ens":2679,"requests":5}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"0fb50bb9d8ceacd27a311f477615e9ed6eb0a53ff08b3e319f2a9e66e52f17e6"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":309379,"output_tokens":5894,"requests":10}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend AC2's check to assert the failure disposition, not just the message: on an unsatisfiable pin, verify `current` is unchanged and the reject-streak counter incremented.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2 disposition: 'the candidate is rejected at its own uv-select stage, current is left untouched, the streak increments, and the next hourly tick retries'","The check only asserts 'the message names all three facts' and 'it selects that uv' — no assertion on current-untouched or streak-increment"],"finding":"AC2 asserts a specific failure DISPOSITION (soft retry: candidate rejected at its own uv-select stage, current left untouched, streak increments, next tick retries) but its stated 'Checked by' clause only verifies the failure MESSAGE content and the satisfiable-pin selection — it does not verify the disposition (that current is untouched and the streak increments) in the resolver harness.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdff6b787cdc905cb","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC2 'Checked by running the resolver against a checkout whose pin no local uv satisfies...'","norm_id":"ne46699b6902002b4","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A resolver bug that emits the correct message but also clobbers `current` or fails to increment the streak would pass the stated check while breaking the promised self-healing behaviour."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to AC2's check: after running the resolver against the unsatisfiable-pin checkout, assert the prior `current` sha is unchanged and the reject-streak value increased by one.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State in AC4 what origin/main the build-stale signal compares against (live `git ls-remote` vs. a local remote-tracking ref vs. the updater's own last-fetched pin) and argue why that source is not itself stale on a box whose updater has stopped fetching.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["build_drift.detect_drift takes a caller-supplied `pinned_sha` and performs no fetch/ls-remote (build_drift.py:147-192)","The sibling advisory module doctor_mcp_client.py is documented 'pure and OS-agnostic ... no subprocess, no network' and the ticket comment says the build-freshness module 'reads no environment at all'","AC4's proof runs 'against a synthetic state directory and a throwaway git repo' — a test repo's origin/main is set up locally and never goes stale, so the test cannot exercise a stale-local-ref host","AC4 text names 'origin/main' but never states whether it resolves it via a live `git ls-remote`, a local remote-tracking ref, or the last fetched pin"],"finding":"AC4's build-stale signal does not name the source of the origin/main reference it compares the published build against; if the live-host scan reads a locally-cached refs/remotes/origin/main, that ref is only as fresh as the last successful fetch, and a stalled updater is exactly what fails to fetch — so commits-behind can be understated on the very box the detector is meant to protect.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0457b8f5ee76029f","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC4 — 'the build behind the updater's `current` pointer more than 25 commits behind `origin/main`'","norm_id":"n131db847532c44c6","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["On the failing host the updater has not fetched for 120+ hours, so refs/remotes/origin/main lags reality; build-stale reports far fewer than the true ~201 commits behind and may fall under the 25 threshold, silencing the detector on exactly the incident it targets","A dev box that never runs the updater but has a stale local origin/main gives a misleading count"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Have the build-stale signal resolve origin/main via a bounded, best-effort `git ls-remote origin main` (degrading to silence/unavailable on failure, matching build_drift's advisory contract), OR compare against the updater's own recorded target sha rather than a possibly-stale local ref; whichever is chosen, name it in AC4 and note the failure/degradation behaviour.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["verify command `! grep -q 'Directory not empty' ~/.local/state/rebar-dev/launchd.err.log` greps the unanchored word 'Directory' — it substring-matches (e.g. 'review_Directory'); anchor it (\\b, ^$, or a quoted key like '\"Directory\":')"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make AC1's freshness check race-free by comparing `current/sha` against the origin/main sha the run itself resolved at sync time (e.g. a sha the run records into its log/state), rather than an independently re-sampled `git ls-remote`.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.27,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The check reads `current/sha` and separately runs `git ls-remote origin main` with no capture of the sha the run actually resolved at sync time","AC1's prose says 'equals origin/main at that moment' — acknowledging the instant is load-bearing — but the two operands are sampled at different instants","A prior review round recorded the same concern in the plan-review cache ('Make AC1's freshness check race-free: capture the origin/main sha the run resolved at sync time')"],"finding":"AC1's proof check re-queries the remote independently of the run it is validating (`= \"$(git ls-remote origin main | cut -f1)\"`), so if origin/main advances between the kickstart run's sync and the operator's ls-remote, a correctly-behaving updater fails the equality — a TOCTOU in the acceptance check itself, not in the fix.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2790d45c1b0b2e46","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC1 — `[ \"$(cat ~/.local/state/rebar-dev/current/sha)\" = \"$(git ls-remote origin main | cut -f1)\" ]`","norm_id":"n7126483b583c4804","priority":0.33,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["main receives a commit in the seconds/minutes between the kickstart sync completing and the operator running the ls-remote comparison; current/sha is the previous tip and the check reports failure on a run that did exactly what AC1 requires"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Have the run record the origin/main sha it resolved at sync (e.g. into update.log or a `resolved-target` state file) and assert `current/sha` equals THAT recorded value, so the comparison uses a single point-in-time observation.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alt